{
  "_comment": "Russian (ru) string bundle for the Python board UI. Any key omitted here falls back to the English source in en.json. Keep every key that en.json defines translated so no English leaks into the Russian UI (guarded by test_i18n). The register is informal (ты/твой), as Russian consumer products and Lichess's own Russian UI use. Chess vocabulary: ферзь (never королева), слон, конь, ладья, пешка, король; шах, мат, пат, ничья; рокировка, превращение; белые/чёрные; фигуры for pieces. Lines drawn on the 128px e-paper panel are kept short and broken with an explicit newline. Counted nouns after a number use the 's'/'min' symbol rather than a spelt-out noun, because Russian needs four different endings and the board t() has no plurals. Two placeholders are filled with a nominative colour label from chess.color.* ('Белые'/'Чёрные'), which no Russian verb governs, so lichess.started and game.resign_color label the side instead of inflecting it.",
